abstract: >-
  The democratization of generative artificial intelligence between 2025 and 2026 has expanded
  the enterprise attack surface beyond the network perimeter into statistical weights, inference
  pipelines, and biometric trust models. This research monograph synthesizes threat intelligence,
  empirical jurisdictional vulnerabilities in India (such as digital arrest extortion and Video-KYC
  injection attacks), and regulatory vacuums across the IT Act 2000 and DPDP Act 2023. It develops
  an adapted 4-layer Trusted Digital Exchange (TDE) framework underpinned by NIST SP 800-207 Zero Trust
  Architecture, unifying C2PA cryptographic provenance, multimodal detection, explainable dynamic trust
  scoring, and institutional continuous governance.
